{"units": [{"id": "hamartano-quote9", "translation": "And having erred in many things, you set nothing right in your mind."}, {"id": "hamartano-quote10", "translation": "He errs in something (thus the Scorialensis codex: τοι [in something] Parisinus A) and is wiser than a wise man."}, {"id": "hamartia-orth1", "translation": "sin, error"}, {"id": "hamartia-def1", "translation": "sin, error"}, {"id": "hamartia-quote1", "translation": "For such a sin they must pay the penalty to the gods."}, {"id": "hamartia-quote2", "translation": "He himself may reap the fruit of his own mind's error."}, {"id": "hamartia-quote3", "translation": "The ancient sins of this house."}, {"id": "hamartia-quote4", "translation": "The gifts are less than the sin."}, {"id": "hamartinoos-orth1", "translation": "erring in mind, mad"}, {"id": "hamartinoos-def1", "translation": "erring in mind, mad"}, {"id": "hamartinoos-quote1", "translation": "From there Io flees, erring in mind."}, {"id": "hamartion-orth1", "translation": "sin, error"}, {"id": "hamartion-def1", "translation": "sin, error"}, {"id": "hamartion-quote1", "translation": "Twin sins of lamentation."}, {"id": "hamartion-quote2", "translation": "The sons of Priam paid double for their sins."}, {"id": "amauros-orth1", "translation": "dim, obscure, uncertain; ignoble; gloomy"}, {"id": "amauros-def1", "translation": "dim, obscure, uncertain"}, {"id": "amauros-def2", "translation": "ignoble"}, {"id": "amauros-def3", "translation": "gloomy"}, {"id": "amauros-quote1", "translation": "He speaks having learned from an obscure report."}, {"id": "amauros-quote2", "translation": "The Erinyes, in time, make him who is fortunate without justice dim."}, {"id": "amauros-quote3", "translation": "From a dim mind."}, {"id": "amauros-quote4", "translation": "From a dim mind."}, {"id": "amauroo-orth1", "translation": "to make dim, to obscure"}, {"id": "amauroo-def1", "translation": "to make dim, to obscure"}, {"id": "amauroo-note1", "translation": "where Blomfield reads κάτοχα μαυροῦσθαι [to be dimmed, held down], which form is read as the meter demands at Ag. 296, Eum. 359."}, {"id": "amauroo-quote1", "translation": "But the opposite of these things, the things that hold down the earth, to be dimmed in darkness,"}, {"id": "amauroo-word1", "translation": "to be dimmed, held down"}, {"id": "amachetos-orth1", "translation": "unconquerable, irresistible"}, {"id": "amachetos-def1", "translation": "unconquerable, irresistible"}, {"id": "amachetos-quote1", "translation": "Like an unconquerable mountain-torrent of water."}, {"id": "amachos-orth1", "translation": "unconquerable, invincible"}, {"id": "amachos-def1", "translation": "unconquerable, invincible"}, {"id": "amachos-quote1", "translation": "The unconquerable wave of the sea."}, {"id": "amachos-quote2", "translation": "Blameless, unconquerable king, godlike Darius."}, {"id": "amachos-quote3", "translation": "Unconquerable grief."}, {"id": "amachos-quote4", "translation": "And the daimon that is unconquerable, unwarlike, unholy."}, {"id": "amao-orth1", "translation": "to reap, to mow"}, {"id": "amao-def1", "translation": "to reap, to mow"}, {"id": "amao-quote1", "translation": "And they who never expected it reaped well."}, {"id": "ambasis-orth1", "translation": "ascent, steps"}, {"id": "ambasis-note1", "translation": "in M πρὸς ἀμβάσεις [to the steps] wrongly ριο προσαμβάσεις [to the approaches]."}, {"id": "ambasis-quote1", "translation": "to the steps"}, {"id": "ambasis-word1", "translation": "to the approaches"}, {"id": "amblyno-orth1", "translation": "to blunt, to dull"}, {"id": "amblyno-def1", "translation": "to blunt, to dull"}, {"id": "amblyno-note1", "translation": "Improperly"}, {"id": "amblyno-note2", "translation": "where the scholiast explains it by ἀπρακτεῖ [is ineffective]."}, {"id": "amblyno-quote1", "translation": "And the oracles are not blunted,"}, {"id": "amblyno-word1", "translation": "is ineffective"}, {"id": "amblys-orth1", "translation": "blunt, dull"}, {"id": "amblys-def1", "translation": "whose force is blunted"}, {"id": "amblys-quote1", "translation": "Not a suppliant's hand, nor one unwashed of blood, but already blunt."}, {"id": "amblopos-orth1", "translation": "dim-sighted, blind"}, {"id": "amblopos-def1", "translation": "dim-sighted, blind"}, {"id": "amblopos-note1", "translation": "a life so full of tears that men's eyes grow dim, as Wellauer interprets it."}, {"id": "amblopos-quote1", "translation": "a life dim with tears"}, {"id": "amboama-orth1", "translation": "cry, shout"}, {"id": "amboama-def1", "translation": "(for ἀναβόημα [a cry]) cry, shout"}, {"id": "amboama-quote1", "translation": "A cry at untimely night sounded from within."}, {"id": "amboama-word1", "translation": "a cry"}, {"id": "amboao-orth1", "translation": "to cry aloud"}, {"id": "amboao-def1", "translation": "(for ἀναβοάω [to cry aloud]) to cry aloud"}, {"id": "amboao-note1", "translation": "I restored it for διαβοάσω [I will shout across]."}, {"id": "amboao-quote1", "translation": "Cry aloud heavily."}, {"id": "amboao-quote2", "translation": "I will shout across"}, {"id": "amboao-word1", "translation": "to cry aloud"}, {"id": "amboao-word2", "translation": "I will shout across"}, {"id": "ambrotos-orth1", "translation": "immortal, divine"}, {"id": "ambrotos-def1", "translation": "immortal, divine"}, {"id": "ambrotos-quote1", "translation": "Of the immortal goddess."}, {"id": "ambon-orth1", "translation": "ridge, edge, rim"}, {"id": "ambon-def1", "translation": "ridge, edge, rim"}, {"id": "ambon-quote1", "translation": "ἄμβωνες [ridges]: the ascents (ἀναβάσεις [ascents] Erotianus p. 86) of the mountains."}, {"id": "amegartos-orth1", "translation": "wretched, unhappy"}, {"id": "amegartos-def1", "translation": "wretched, unhappy"}, {"id": "amegartos-note1", "translation": "Schol. ἀφθόνητον, διὰ τὸ ἀτελές [not to be envied, because of its incompleteness]."}, {"id": "amegartos-quote1", "translation": "For these things are wretched, which Zeus strengthens with his own laws."}, {"id": "amegartos-quote2", "translation": "This wretched flock."}, {"id": "amegartos-word1", "translation": "not to be envied, because of its incompleteness"}, {"id": "ameibo-orth1", "translation": "to exchange, to pass, to answer, to repay"}, {"id": "ameibo-def1", "translation": "to exchange"}, {"id": "ameibo-def2", "translation": "to pass through, to cross"}, {"id": "ameibo-def3", "translation": "to give back, to repay"}, {"id": "ameibo-def4", "translation": "to answer"}, {"id": "ameibo-def5", "translation": "to occupy a place in exchange, to enter"}, {"id": "ameibo-note1", "translation": "where Erfurdt restored ἀμείψει [will exchange] as the meter demands."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote1", "translation": "You will exchange the flower of your complexion."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote2", "translation": "Changing his skin with purple dye."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote3", "translation": "Having crossed the strait of Athamantian Helle."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote4", "translation": "But if I pass through the gates of the courtyard,"}, {"id": "ameibo-quote5", "translation": "Repaying the favor of nurture."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote6", "translation": "Wishing to repay with requital."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote7", "translation": "Answer word with word."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote8", "translation": "Answer all these things with something easy for me to learn."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote9", "translation": "Answer the strangers with respectful words."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote10", "translation": "Answer these things and speak boldly to me."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote11", "translation": "What better land than this will you exchange for?"}, {"id": "ameibo-quote12", "translation": "The oarage, which ever crosses the Acheron, the un-groaning — sacred ship."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote13", "translation": "Soon all-fulfilling time will pass the threshold of the house."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote14", "translation": "Consider and exchange this place."}, {"id": "ameibo-quote15", "translation": "No one of mortals will pass through life unharmed,"}, {"id": "ameibo-word1", "translation": "will exchange"}, {"id": "ameilichos-orth1", "translation": "harsh, unyielding"}, {"id": "ameilichos-def1", "translation": "harsh, unyielding"}]}